Subject: [PATCH KW3/3] key-web: KeyWebURLLoaderFactory serving verified
 unprivileged .swbn bundles with zero install ceremony

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
Copyright 2026 The Key-Origin Web Authors
Target: Chromium 160.0.8176.0 (apply after KW1 and KW2:
        patch -p1 -d src < this.patch)

A minimal, non-network loader for key-web://<kw-id>.key/ that reuses
Chromium's own Signed Web Bundle stack and none of the Isolated Web App
trust machinery.

components/webapps/key_web/url_loading/
  key_web_reader_cache.*
    Releases live at <profile>/Key Web Bundles/<kw-id>.swbn. Nothing is
    installed or registered and no prompt is shown, because nothing is
    trusted: web_app::SignedWebBundleReader::Create(path,
    key-web://<kw-id>.key/, verify_signatures=true) parses the integrity
    block out of process and verifies every signature over SHA-512 of the
    unsigned bundle. Readers are cached per profile and re-verified when the
    file changes (generation-checked, so a stale verification never wins).
  key_web_bundle_validation.*
    On the web_package::SignedWebBundleIntegrityBlock:
      * webBundleId must equal the origin's kw-id;
      * self-certifying identity: some verified signature's public key must
        derive to the kw-id via SignedWebBundleId::CreateForPublicKey(). This
        is checked independently of the process-wide IdentityValidator, so
        IWA key-rotation data can never vouch for a key-web origin;
      * the `keyWeb` attribute must be present (author intent: an IWA bundle
        is never replayed as key-web) with v == 1 and an unsigned seq.
    Every bundle index entry must be same-origin with the key URL.
  key_web_url_loader_factory.*
    GET/HEAD only. Name hosts and bare IDs fail with ERR_INVALID_URL.
    Responses pass through key_web::SetRequiredHeadersForKeyWeb() (KW2) and
    are then re-parsed by the network service, so navigations and workers
    enforce exactly the injected CSP and Connection-Allowlist. Missing
    entries get a synthetic 404 that carries the same policy. Never falls
    back to the network.
  key_web_url_rewrite.*
    BrowserURLHandler: key-web://<kw-id>/ -> key-web://<kw-id>.key/, so one
    key is always exactly one origin.

chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc (all behind kKeyOriginWeb)
  * CreateNonNetworkNavigationURLLoaderFactory: key-web navigations.
  * RegisterNonNetworkWorkerMainResourceURLLoaderFactories: workers, only for
    key-web initiators and locked to that key.
  * RegisterNonNetworkServiceWorkerUpdateURLLoaderFactories: SW scripts.
  * RegisterNonNetworkSubresourceURLLoaderFactories: only for key-web
    initiators, locked to the initiator's key.
  * GetStoragePartitionConfigForSite: one persistent StoragePartition per
    key ("k" + b64(SHA-256(ctx || origin))), never an IWA partition.
  * BrowserURLHandlerCreated: the bare-ID rewrite.

Out of scope (follow-ups): HWM / rollback store and K-SAID KEL validation
(Spec §1.6, §4), name-host resolution and display (Blueprint KW6), capability
grants (KW5).

Tests: components_unittests --gtest_filter='KeyWebBundleValidationTest.*:KeyWebUrlRewriteTest.*'

